{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The custom dual-matmul kernel loses to ROCm’s batched GEMM, so I’m discarding that route. The useful result is narrower: fusing `grad_query` is beneficial for 128- and 211-token rows, while tuned single-wave softmax is clearly best through 256 tokens. I’m measuring the remaining exact row lengths and batch regimes before locking the dispatch."}}
