{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The second verification is clean and materially faster, especially at high batch counts. The remaining short-sequence cost is now the standalone `grad_key` launch. For the 128×128 case, the entire per-head derivative matrix is only 32 KiB in bfloat16, so I’m testing a one-program-per-head kernel that computes the derivative and both matmuls together; this is the one regime where full fusion can plausibly stay on-chip."}}
