{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"ROCm’s batched GEMM remains decisively faster than ordinary Triton tiles, so I’m keeping it for long rows. There is one promising middle regime left: for square rows around 211–256, a single block can stream 16 query rows at a time, emit `grad_query`, and retain the entire `grad_key` accumulator across the stream. I’m testing that design; it preserves one-pass input reads and removes both library launches."}}
